 "tableLines": [
  {
   "day": 10,
   "line": "◈ FLASHBACK — Nora's Drawing\nKitchen table, burnt pancakes. You told her the sun needed holding, and she took you literally — drew you carrying it with both hands. She was six. The sky changed three weeks later."
  },
  {
   "day": 11,
   "line": "\"Your understanding is... deepening! We can see it! Like watching a seed decide to be a tree! Beautiful! Profitable!\""
  },
  {
   "day": 18,
   "line": "Deeper knowledge: Burdock. Uses: starchy root vegetable. Dig first-year plants (no flower stalk). (+5 health when eaten). All uses known: food: first-year roots only — dig deep, peel, cook like carrots; medicine: root tea, traditional blood purifier; fiber: tough stalk fiber for rough cordage."
  },
  {
   "day": 39,
   "line": "✨ Ability gained: Fusion Reactor (L1). The System installs your fusion pellet — properly, inside you. You never need to eat again: the pellet covers your metabolism, and your strikes and abilities burn with a steady reactor fire (1.25x, always on). One reactor per world, and it never comes out: not unslotted, not un-taught, not surrendered. Death is the only uninstall. But the hunger is gone, and "
  },
  {
   "day": 42,
   "line": "The village feels it before they understand it: Haven isn't just Haven anymore. Saul speaks at Emberhold's table now — earned, not appointed. And the other fire is watching what Haven does FIRST."
  },
  {
   "day": 44,
   "line": "The village feels it before they understand it: Haven isn't just Haven anymore. Saul speaks at Stonebridge's table now — earned, not appointed. And the other fire is watching what Haven does FIRST."
  },
  {
   "day": 48,
   "line": "The village feels it before they understand it: Haven isn't just Haven anymore. Saul speaks at Thornfield's table now — earned, not appointed. And the other fire is watching what Haven does FIRST."
  },
  {
   "day": 68,
   "line": "◈ FLASHBACK — Vanesa's Drawing\nKitchen table, burnt pancakes. You told her the sun needed holding, and she took you literally — drew you carrying it with both hands. She was six. The sky changed three weeks later."
  },
  {
   "day": 90,
   "line": "◈ THE TABLE — the ring of pale light flickers at the edge of the sky... and does not come. Not yet. The table is being set for those whose deeds are done, and yours are not done. The ledger still wants: the food-thesis deeds. The climb is not over."
  },
  {
   "day": 94,
   "line": "◈ SYSTEM: \"Oh. OH. Do you feel that? That's the whole PLANET leaning in. ...There's a table, little fires. A big one. Far away. And it is LOOKING at you. Give it a season worth judging.\""
  },
  {
   "day": 105,
   "line": "🖱️ The Algorithm trailers its next move at Desmond — the predictable get countered."
  },
  {
